<title>USA: U.S. Q3 GDP final estimate rose 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q3 GDP final estimate rose 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce seasonally adjusted GDP data on a chain-weighted basis. Following are annualized percent changes from prior quarters, in 1992 chain dollars.</p>
<p>    -			     Q3-F---Q3-P---Q2-F---1995</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	2.1    2.0    4.7    2.0</p>
<p> Final Sales Domest.Product  0.5    0.4    4.1    2.4</p>
<p> GDP Price Index		 2.0    1.9    2.2    2.5</p>
<p> Implicit Price Deflator     1.7    1.6    1.8    2.5</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	     0.5    0.6    3.4    2.3</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		 -2.6   -2.0   11.4    3.2</p>
<p> -Nondurable Goods	     0.4    0.3    1.3    2.3</p>
<p>Pct Change,'92 chain dollars: Q3-F---Q3-P---Q2-F---1995</p>
<p> Consumer Spending-Services  1.3    1.3    2.7    2.2</p>
<p> Business Investment	  17.5   16.9    3.8    9.5</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   -5.2   -5.9   16.3   -2.3</p>
<p> Exports of Goods/Svcs	-0.9   -0.9    5.6    8.9</p>
<p> Imports of Goods/Svcs	 9.3    9.9    9.9    8.0</p>
<p> Govt.Purchases/Investment  -0.6   -0.2    7.7   Unch</p>
<p> -Federal			 -3.5   -3.4    9.4   -3.6</p>
<p> -State and Local		1.1    1.7    6.7    2.4</p>
<p>Note: Advance (A) is first estimate, Preliminary (P) is second estimate, and Final (F) is last estimate for the quarter.  </p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted annual rates, in blns of '92 chain dollars:</p>
<p>    -				Q3-F-----Q3-P-----Q2-F----1995</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product   6,928.4  6,926.2  6,892.6  6,742.9</p>
<p> Final Sales Dom.Product  6,892.7  6,892.1  6,884.7  6,708.9</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	  4,693.5  4,694.3  4,687.6  4,577.8</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		 611.6    612.5    615.6    579.8</p>
<p> -NonDurable Goods	  1,442.2  1,442.0  1,440.9  1,421.9</p>
<p> -Services		    2,640.6  2,640.7  2,632.3  2,577.0</p>
<p> Business Investment	  781.4    780.4    750.5    714.3</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   277.8    277.3    281.5    262.8</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.  </p>
<p> Blns of '92 chain dollars:     Q3-F-----Q3-P-----Q2-F-----1995</p>
<p> Inventory Change		34.5     32.8	7.1     33.1</p>
<p> -NonFarm			  34.6     33.0     11.7     37.2</p>
<p> -Farm			     -0.4     -0.5     -5.1     -4.7</p>
<p> Net Exports Goods/Svcs    -137.4   -138.8   -114.7   -107.6</p>
<p> -Exports			 816.1    816.1    817.9    775.4</p>
<p> -Imports			 953.5    954.8    932.6    883.0</p>
<p> Government Purchases     1,276.1  1,277.4  1,278.2  1,260.2</p>
<p> -Federal			 469.3    469.3    473.4    472.3</p>
<p> -State and Local	     807.7    809.0    805.5    788.6</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.  </p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected the final estimate of third quarter GDP growth to show a 2.0 percent increase, the price index to be up 1.9 percent and the implicit deflator to rise 1.6 percent.</p>
